==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|kweþanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|gʷet-|lang=ine-pro}} (cf. {{proto|cel-pro|bet-lo-|mouth|lang=}} in Old Irish {{term|bél|lang=sga}}). Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|qwetha|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|queþan|lang=osx}}, Old Dutch {{term|quethan|lang=odt}} (Middle Dutch {{term|quedden|lang=dum}}), Old High German {{term|quedan|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|kveða|lang=non}} (Icelandic {{term|kveða|lang=is}}, Swedish {{term|kväda|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌵𐌹𐌸𐌰𐌽|sc=Goth|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkweθɑn/|lang=ang}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"kweTAn/|lang=ang}}

